course: dictionary
lesson: 1995
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word con can mean a trick, the bad points of something, a prison worker, or a big fan event. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Those words are the context, and they leave clues.
explain: «A con is a trick that takes something from people who did not agree to be fooled.» The clues are trick, takes and fooled. So con means a trick that cheats someone. Test it: swap in trick and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «We looked at the pros and cons before we decided.» Pros are the good points, so cons must be the bad points. The word is not about a trick here. Always ask which meaning fits the sentence, then check your choice by reading the whole sentence again.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A con (noun) is a trick to cheat someone, usually to get their money.
fact: To con (verb) means to trick someone into believing something false or giving you something.
fact: Cons can mean the disadvantages or bad points, as in «pros and cons».
fact: Informal meanings: con can be short for convict (a person in prison), or a con can be a big fan meeting, like a comic con.
exercise: «A con is a trick that takes something from people who did not agree to be fooled.» What is a con here? | A happy surprise party | A bright star in the night sky | *A trick to cheat someone
exercise: «We looked at the pros and cons before we decided.» What are the cons? | The loud noises in the hall | *The bad points | The prizes you can win
exercise: Ellie gets a message: «You have won a prize! Send us your password.» Her teacher says it is a con. What does con mean here? | A fun fan event for comics | *A trick to get your password or money | A happy present from a friend
test: «He tried to con his little brother into doing his chores.» What does con mean here? | To help someone with a job | *To trick someone into doing something for you | To sing very loudly
test: At a comic con, fans dress up as their favourite heroes. What is a comic con? | *A big fan meeting | A kind of cheat | A school trip to the museum
exam: «She saw through the con before she handed over her money.» Which meaning of con fits? | A big fan meeting | *A trick to cheat someone | The bad points of a plan | A person in prison
